hifiberry-webui (0.21.4) stable; urgency=medium

  * Players: stop two conflicting players being enabled at once. Players
    that cannot coexist (two Spotify Connect endpoints) were shown as
    independent toggles, so both could be left enabled -- systemd's
    Conflicts= only stops them running at the same instant, so both would
    start at boot and whichever won the race stopped the other, giving a
    different player on different boots. Enabling one now switches the
    other off first and says so. The conflict is read from the player
    descriptor's conflicts_with (needs configurator 2.17.1) and applied
    symmetrically, since only one side of a pair declares it.

