hifiberry-webui (0.21.3) stable; urgency=medium

  * Extensions: stop the install dialog hanging for ever when its job
    disappears. Jobs live only in config-server's memory, so a restart
    while one is running makes its id 404 permanently -- but the poll
    caught every error alike and re-armed its timer unconditionally, so a
    job that could never return looked identical to one still in progress.
    The dialog sat on the last phase it saw, typically "Configuring", with
    Close disabled, while the operation had in fact already completed.
    A 404 now ends tracking with a clear message, and a run of other
    failures gives up after 15s rather than never.
  * Extensions: refresh the list on any terminal outcome, not just success,
    so an abandoned job still shows the package's real installed state.

