hifiberry-webui (0.21.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * Player settings: add support for credential fields (type 'secret'). Plugins
    can now request a credential via a player setting. The credential is
    rendered as a write-only masked input and never stored in or returned from
    the setting value. A Set / Not set indicator shows whether a credential
    is stored, and a Clear button allows removal. Typed values are held
    transiently and dropped if the panel closes by any route (Cancel, Save,
    collapse, or panel unmount), so an abandoned credential is never silently
    written later.
  * Player settings: fix cross-player settings clobbering. Saving one player's
    settings no longer overwrites another player's unsaved edits (including
    in-flight credentials) if both panels are open at the same time.
  * Player settings: fix credential leaks through panel close paths. Collapsing
    the panel via the expand caret or closing after a failed save no longer
    leaves a typed credential in memory.

