hifiberry-webui (0.20.16) stable; urgency=medium

  * CSS custom properties, part 1 of the undefined-token cleanup: define
    the ~20 tokens that were already used with exactly one, consistent
    hardcoded fallback everywhere in the codebase (--color-border-light,
    --card-background, --font-mono, etc.) as that literal value in
    colors.module.scss/colors.scss, so the value lives in one place
    instead of being repeated at every call site. Deliberately given the
    same light and dark value - a hardcoded fallback is theme-blind by
    definition, so it already rendered identically in both themes; a
    real dark value is a separate design decision for a follow-up.
  * Remove the 15 dead --tblr-* custom properties (Tabler UI Kit
    tokens) from dsp-programs.vue - this project has never depended on
    Tabler, so these always resolved to their hardcoded fallback and
    never will resolve to anything else. Replaced with that literal
    value directly; no behaviour change.
  * No visual change: verified by diffing the built CSS before/after -
    every pre-existing custom property is byte-identical, the only
    additions are the 20 new tokens (matching their prior fallback
    exactly) and the dsp-programs.vue literal substitutions.

