hifiberry-webui (0.20.6) stable; urgency=medium

  * Cover art: stop retrying an image the browser has already rejected. A cover
    art URL that 404s made onImageError run the fallback chain, but the metadata
    fallback was routed through loadCoverArt(), whose cache is keyed on
    title/artist/album - so it returned the cached broken result and the
    fallback URL was discarded. Toggling the loading state then recreated the
    <img> with the same dead src, firing the error handler again, forever. The
    component now tracks failed URLs, advances through the remaining candidates,
    and falls back to the placeholder once they are exhausted.

 -- HiFiBerry <support@hifiberry.com>  Mon, 03 Aug 2026 10:00:00 +0000

hifiberry-webui (0.20.5) stable; urgency=medium

  * Web Services: route the Spotify and Last.fm APIs through apiFetch. Both
    connection flows are risky-tier apart from their /status reads
    (/spotify/create_session, /login/*, /poll/*, /tokens, /logout and
    /lastfm/auth, /prepare_complete_auth, /complete_auth, /disconnect), but
    src/api/spotify.ts and src/api/lastfm.ts still used plain fetch. Clicking
    Connect therefore failed on the gateway's 401 with no password prompt at
    all, and sent no X-CSRF-Token, so it failed even for a signed-in user.
    Reported at support.hifiberry.com/forum/c/software/10860 and /10861.
  * Room EQ: startRoomEQRecording and startRoomMeasure now prompt as well.
    Microphone recording and room measurement are deliberately risky, so
    measuring a room was impossible without a password prompt appearing.
  * The filter-chain view (/api/config/v1/pipewire/filtergraph), the bare
    config collection read and getConfigValue(secure=true) now prompt instead
    of throwing a raw 401.
  * Bluetooth pairing, unpair, the settings toggles and passkey confirmation
    go through apiFetch; /bluetooth/* is only ok-tier for GET, so every
    Bluetooth write hit the same dead end.
  * The remaining device API calls (player, volume, library, inputs, coverart,
    pipewire, dsptoolkit, system) are routed through apiFetch too, so they keep
    working if a manifest reclassifies them or protection is set to "all".
    Third-party endpoints (MusicBrainz, radio-browser.info) stay on plain
    fetch, since they are not behind the gateway.
  * Adds src/api/__tests__/noRawFetch.test.ts, which fails the build if any new
    call to a device API base URL uses plain fetch, plus spotify, lastfm,
    bluetooth and riskyEndpoints suites covering the challenge, retry, csrf and
    cancel paths.

 -- HiFiBerry <support@hifiberry.com>  Sat, 01 Aug 2026 08:00:00 +0000

hifiberry-webui (0.20.4) stable; urgency=medium

