hifiberry-webui (0.20.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * Add the security / password-protection UI for the system-wide auth gateway.
    A new Security settings page sets or changes the device password and chooses
    how much it covers (risky operations only, or everything). Risky API calls
    now go through an apiFetch wrapper that, on a 401, prompts for the password
    (SecurityPrompt modal) and retries; everyday music playback, volume and
    library browsing never prompt. The nginx server block is wired for the
    auth_request gateway.
  * After a page reload the session cookie is still valid but the in-memory CSRF
    token is gone; the first risky write now silently rehydrates the token from
    the live session instead of re-prompting for the password.
  * Security page spans the full content width (matching the other settings
    pages) and fixes form inputs that rendered invisible because they referenced
    theme CSS variables that do not exist.

